# Trust and flow

- **Trust level**: `trusted` or `untrusted`, per event for one principal's
  agents on one node: derived by the trust policy from the event's provenance,
  origin (whether recorded on this node or ingested⟦f:segment-exchange⟧, or received⟦/f⟧⟦f:bundle-import⟧⟦f:export-bundles⟧, or
  imported⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧), recorder and writer, the deployment mode recorded with the event,
  the node's key set⟦f:work-rooms⟧⟦f:shared-rooms⟧, whether the event's room is foreign to that principal⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:stamps⟧, and that principal's
  stamps⟦f:trust-grants⟧ and trust grants⟦/f⟧ as its writer logs carry them⟦/f⟧ (I10). The free text a
  cut or neutral principal act carries, such as a stated reason, is untrusted
  whatever its event's trust level (OWN-11).
- **Trusted sources**: I2's trusted sources as PRV-02 applies them⟦f:work-rooms⟧⟦f:shared-rooms⟧, which RCL-10
  narrows in a foreign room⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧: this node's `operator` and structural events and
  those the predecessors of its own device seats, however far back, wrote (Seat
  key, Node), the
  `harness_meta` events its hook handlers recorded (Hook), and the `user` events
  they recorded (Turn) while the deployment mode is `interactive`, all trusted only on this
  node⟦f:principal-keys⟧; and, once PRV-10 ships, principal acts signed by a device key the
  agent's principal certified, ⟦f:conversation⟧posts and ⟦/f⟧pins written from a device seat such a
  key certified, within that key's scope⟦f:stamps⟧, a pin version its principal stamped⟦/f⟧⟦f:trust-grants⟧,
  and for that agent the ⟦f:conversation⟧posts and ⟦/f⟧pins a trust grant of its principal covers⟦/f⟧⟦f:work-rooms⟧⟦f:shared-rooms⟧,
  none of them in a foreign room but the pins⟦f:stamps⟧ and stamps⟦/f⟧ Foreign room names⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧.
  Everything else is untrusted, and so is the free text a cut or neutral
  principal act carries (OWN-11).
- **Deployment mode**: `interactive` (a person types at the harness) or
  `automation` (a pipeline does), set per node (PRV-02, `node.deployment_mode`).
- **Trust policy**: The rule that derives each event's trust level (PRV-02).
- **Trust mark**: The sign beside an item saying where it came from and whether
  it is trusted, from §9.7.6's closed set (VIEW-07).
- **Taint**: The trust level a derived artifact, or an output built from events
  (a recall result⟦f:compute-kernel⟧, kernel output⟦/f⟧⟦f:export-bundles⟧, an exported bundle, rendering or trusted-only
  export⟦/f⟧), inherits: untrusted when any event it derives from is untrusted,
  except for its sanitized structural fields.
⟦f:rule-levels⟧- **Recall taint**: A run's mark after it recalls untrusted content, or
  inherited from the delegating run (OWN-24), which tightens the rule levels of
  the action classes SEC-13 configures as sensitive (OWN-10).⟦/f⟧
- **Principal surface**: An authenticated client where principal acts are taken:
  ⟦f:browser-room-view⟧the browser room view under SEC-20, `parinn ui` started at a terminal that
  no run's tool process started, ⟦/f⟧the CLI or TUI at a terminal that no
  run's tool process started⟦f:paired-phone⟧, or a paired phone⟦f:principal-keys⟧ within its scope⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧. A CLI
  or TUI call from inside a run is the agent's own tool call: never a principal
  act and never a device seat's room act, and what it returns is recall,
  enveloped, whatever its output (OWN-02, Recall).⟦f:browser-room-view⟧ A browser on the principal's
  phone⟦f:peer-sync⟧⟦f:paired-phone⟧, without the peer component,⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧ reaches the room view only as the browser
  room view, through the principal's own tunnel, which is the principal's tool
  outside ParleyInn's components (I4).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:presence-proof⟧- **Presence proof**: A hardware-backed, user-verified proof of a person's
  presence, bound to one widening act (OWN-11).⟦/f⟧
- **Recall**: An agent's call to a **recall tool**, which is any tool ParleyInn
  serves to an agent: every MCP tool (§9.2), such as `event_search`, `room_get`⟦f:facilitator⟧,
  `room_summary_get`⟦/f⟧⟦f:delegation-grants⟧, `delegation_get`⟦/f⟧⟦f:compute-kernel⟧, `kernel_exec` with its built-ins
  (CMP-03)⟦/f⟧ or a `room_<act>` tool, and any CLI or TUI call from inside a run
  (OWN-02, OWN-12). Everything ParleyInn returns to such a call is recall,
  whatever its output: enveloped, and recorded as a recall event (RCL-07).
  Pull-only, and it defaults to the agent's current run. A recall that returns a
  pin returns its range links. A recall tool that stops at its per-call
  cap returns a **continuation cursor** (`next_cursor`); passed back as
  `cursor`, it continues without gap or overlap (RCL-03).
- **Closed path**: One of the ways I2 lists by which ParleyInn writes to an agent
  without the agent's recall: restore blocks⟦f:notices⟧, opt-in notices⟦/f⟧⟦f:held-requests⟧, OWN-04's⟦f:away-policy⟧ and
  OWN-07's⟦/f⟧ templates⟦/f⟧ and compaction guidance⟦f:launcher⟧; on a principal act recorded at
  that time, through the harness's own input, principal-typed text, a fixed
  template referencing ids⟦f:endorsement⟧⟦f:conversation⟧ or an endorsed post⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧⟦f:delegation-grants⟧; a delegated task under its
  grants⟦/f⟧⟦f:trust-grants⟧; and what a trust grant covers⟦/f⟧. No other write to an agent exists (I2),
  and data leaves the machine through them only as the harness sends them to its
  model (I4).
- **Recall scope**: `run` or `room`⟦f:work-rooms⟧, or `rooms`⟦f:shared-rooms⟧, or a foreign room named in the
  call⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧ (RCL-05). A wider scope is said to extend recall; "widening" belongs to
  acts.
⟦f:endorsement⟧- **Endorsement**: The principal act of a principal with a seat in the room,
  sending a post's text, exactly as the principal confirmed it after any edit,
  to one of the principal's own agents, inside a fixed template naming the
  author's seat key fingerprint and the post's address (OWN-08).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:trust-grants⟧- **Trust grant**: A principal's widening act trusting another principal's key
  for its own agents, in one room or everywhere. It covers that principal's
  ⟦f:conversation⟧posts and ⟦/f⟧pins written from device seats a device key of that principal
  certified⟦f:principal-keys⟧, within that key's device scope⟦/f⟧, never ⟦f:conversation⟧a cross-room post shown in
  another room, ⟦/f⟧run seats⟦f:access-tokens⟧, token-key-only nodes⟦/f⟧⟦f:facilitator⟧, the facilitator's device seat
  or room summaries⟦/f⟧; never in a foreign room⟦f:conversation⟧; and a post it
  covers reaches only the grantor's agents whose run has a seat in the post's
  room, inside OWN-29's template: wording ParleyInn ships, filled only with ids, key
  fingerprints, addresses and that post's text⟦/f⟧⟦f:service-accounts⟧. A grant naming a service account whose certificate or managed-policy
  listing, standing or revoked, marks it as relaying text others wrote, whose
  listing is unmarked, or that no standing certificate or listing covers, is
  refused; one naming any other service account shows a warning⟦/f⟧ (OWN-29). Its
  revocation is cut.⟦/f⟧
- **Delegation**: One agent handing another a delegated task: its subagent⟦f:delegation-grants⟧, or,
  under a delegation grant, another agent of the same principal on this node⟦f:segment-exchange⟧ or
  on another of its nodes⟦/f⟧⟦f:acceptance-grants⟧, or another principal's agent⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧ (OWN-23 to OWN-26).
- **Delegated task**: The text of a delegation: a subagent's from its harness⟦f:delegation-grants⟧,
  any other in OWN-24's template⟦/f⟧. In the delegate's run it is recorded with
  `assistant` provenance, as the delegating run's text, never as a `user` event
  (Turn).
⟦f:delegation-grants⟧- **Delegate report**: What a delegate returns, recorded on the delegating side
  so it stays in the delegating run's recall scope (OWN-24), enveloped: through
  `delegation_get`, except a subagent's, which its harness returns as untrusted
  `subagent_result` (OWN-25). Every delegate report is untrusted⟦f:segment-exchange⟧; one from
  another node⟦f:acceptance-grants⟧ or principal⟦/f⟧ stays attributed to the delegate's seat key (I8)⟦/f⟧.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:delegation-grants⟧- **Delegation grant**: The delegating principal's widening act naming who may
  delegate, to which targets⟦f:rule-levels⟧, at what rule level⟦/f⟧, within what **delegation
  budget** (its cap in spend), how many delegates at once, how deep, and until
  when (OWN-23); past that expiry the delegating node refuses a delegation under
  it⟦f:principal-keys⟧, and its expire act ends it⟦/f⟧.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:acceptance-grants⟧- **Acceptance grant**: The receiving principal's widening act on its own node,
  naming the delegating principal, the targets⟦f:rule-levels⟧, the maximum rule level⟦/f⟧⟦f:delegation-grants⟧, the
  delegation budget⟦/f⟧ and the expiry (OWN-26), which ends it as a delegation
  grant's does. Delegation to another principal's agent needs both a delegation
  grant and an acceptance grant.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:held-requests⟧- **Permission grant**: The grant that lets an approved action pass again when
  the harness next raises it at its permission prompt (OWN-07).⟦f:delegation-grants⟧ Separate from
  ⟦f:trust-grants⟧trust and ⟦/f⟧delegation grants.⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧
⟦f:notices⟧- **Notice allowance, notice opt-in**: The owner's per-room allowance and the
  agent's principal's opt-in. An opt-in notice needs both.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:rule-levels⟧- **Rule level**: For each action class (a kind of tool action, such as edits,
  commands or network use), one of, loosest to tightest: act without asking, act
  when told, ask first, hand off (OWN-10). A maximum rule level is the loosest
  allowed.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:store-protection⟧- **Quota**: A limit on storage or events, per room⟦f:peer-sync⟧, writer received from
  a peer, peer⟦/f⟧⟦f:git-tracking⟧, worktree checkpoint⟦/f⟧ or node, that the node's principal or managed
  policy sets (ADM-15); reaching it never drops, truncates or deletes an event:
  it is counted and shown (I6).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:delegation-grants⟧- **Spend**: What runs cost in model tokens or money⟦f:store-protection⟧; no quota limits it until
  OQ-26 closes⟦/f⟧.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:away-policy⟧- **Away policy**: A principal's opt-in choice of what an unanswered held
  request does while it is on: keep going, pause or stop (OWN-07). Only that
  principal act sets it, never a settings key.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:sandbox-risk⟧- **Residual risk**: One of the risks §6.1 lists for an unconfined run.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:sandbox-risk⟧- **Sandbox state**: What confines a run, its policy digest, and which residual
  risks it blocks, recorded from outside the sandbox, where the agent cannot
  write (OWN-22).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:sandbox-risk⟧- **Risk acceptance**: The principal's act accepting the residual risks a run
  leaves open (OWN-22).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:held-requests⟧- **Hand-off, hand-back**: An agent passes control to its principal as a held
  request; the principal returns control with a note⟦f:git-tracking⟧ and a worktree checkpoint⟦/f⟧
  (OWN-20).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:launcher⟧- **Run controls**: Steer, interrupt, pause, resume and stop: principal acts on
  a run. **Terminal takeover**, the principal typing in the harness's terminal
  the launcher hosts, is the harness's own channel, never a principal act
  (OWN-02, OWN-19): the person's keystrokes are the harness's own input from
  that terminal, which the launcher hosts but never carries, so what the
  launcher carries into the harness's input stays text the core built (I4).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:launcher⟧- **Fixed template**: Wording ParleyInn ships, filled only with ids, counts, version
  numbers, key fingerprints, addresses and the principal-typed⟦f:endorsement⟧, endorsed⟦/f⟧⟦f:delegation-grants⟧ or
  delegated⟦/f⟧ text⟦f:trust-grants⟧⟦f:conversation⟧, or the text of a post a trust grant covers⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧, its requirement
  names; **principal-typed text** is text a principal typed at a principal
  surface for that act.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:launcher⟧- **Correction, retry**: ⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧After a verdict: ⟦/f⟧principal-typed text in a fixed
  template⟦f:git-tracking⟧, or a new run from a worktree checkpoint⟦/f⟧ (OWN-28).⟦/f⟧
- **Counter**: A count of dropped, rejected, redacted, truncated, coalesced,
  timed-out or failed operations of one kind, each also written to the **audit
  log**, the node's append-only log of ParleyInn's own operations (OPS-01), shown on
  Health until acknowledged (`parinn counter ack`, I6, OPS-03).
- **Canary**: `parinn canary`'s end-to-end test: it writes a **canary event**
  through the hook path and recalls it through the MCP server (OPS-04).
⟦f:landmarks⟧- **Stat**: A count derived from the record within a recall scope, such as
  events, runs, compactions or recalls, read through `stat_list` (RCL-01).⟦/f⟧
- **Run status**: A run's one status from §9.7.1's closed set (one waiting on
  its principal, such as on a permission request, is Asking⟦f:needs-you⟧, never Needs you⟦/f⟧), with its **freshness mark**, which
  says how current the run's events are on this node, whether hooks still arrive
  (`unrecorded`), or that it is an ingested run (`ingested`)⟦f:room-view-surfaces⟧; `stuck?` is a
  watchdog observation⟦/f⟧ (VIEW-04); time-relative freshness marks are computed
  where shown, never derived artifacts.
⟦f:room-status⟧- **Room status**: A room's one status from §9.7.2's closed set, such as
  Running, Quiet or Ready for review. It is computed where shown from room
  state, the heads, landings⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧ and check states⟦/f⟧ of the branches it names, its
  runs' statuses and their freshness marks. It is never recorded and never set
  directly; OWN-21's ready and abandoned marks feed it.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:needs-you⟧- **Queue class**: One of Needs you's classes Q1 to Q4, which set its order
  (§9.7.4, VIEW-05).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:needs-you⟧- **Focus set**: The rooms a principal marks to come first in Needs you, changed
  by a recorded neutral principal act⟦f:peer-sync⟧, so every device shows one order⟦/f⟧.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:room-status⟧- **Open room**: A room with no ready mark whose branch heads still stand
  (OWN-21) and no abandoned mark, that names no branch or names one that has not
  landed.⟦/f⟧
⟦f:results-and-verdicts⟧- **Exposure**: Of a branch, the untrusted and flagged items its runs read⟦f:rule-levels⟧ and
  their recall taint⟦/f⟧ (VIEW-13).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:room-status⟧- **Overlap**: Runs in two open rooms editing one file⟦f:needs-you⟧, which raises a Needs you
  item for each room's owner until that owner acknowledges it for that room⟦/f⟧
  (LANE-13).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:segment-exchange⟧- **Fork**: Either of two events one writer sealed at one seq, both kept for
  forensics; the node's principal chooses which fork to keep (PEER-10).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:conversation⟧⟦f:peer-sync⟧- **Presence hint**: An ephemeral sign that a seat is connected, or typing (a
  **typing hint**), never stored in the record (PEER-09).⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧
⟦f:room-view-surfaces⟧- **Watchdog observation**: ParleyInn's note, computed where shown and never
  recorded, that a run looks stuck, shown as the `stuck?` freshness mark; it
  never starts or resumes a turn (OWN-09).⟦/f⟧
⟦f:room-view-surfaces⟧- **Petname**: A name the person viewing chose for a key or a room, never one
  another principal sent (VIEW-07).⟦f:needs-you⟧ Notifications carry a room's petname, else
  its id.⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧
